        "type": "User"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "`let` is not hoisted to the top of the function. Meaning you can now safely have `let` variables scoped inside `if` and `while` without any collision risk with a variable defined in a higher scope.\n",
      "date": 1447325637,
      "id": 156072022,
      "reactions": {},
      "user": {
        "avatar": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/283419",
        "id": 283419,
        "login": "pixelastic",
        "type": "User"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "OK, so it's a way to safeguard us from possible errors when using `var` in an inappropriate way?\n",
